---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { page, breadcrumb } from '../lib/seo';
const schema = [
  page('AboutPage', { site:Astro.site, path:'/about', name:'About Ground Floor', description:'What Ground Floor tests and where its authority stops.' }),
  breadcrumb(Astro.site, [{ name:'Ground Floor', path:'/' }, { name:'About', path:'/about' }]),
];
---
<Base title="About Ground Floor" description="What Ground Floor tests and where its authority stops." appearance="light" schema={schema}>
  <header class="gf-page-hero"><div class="gf-shell"><p class="gf-eyebrow">About</p><h1 class="gf-display mt-4">A practical test bench for small professional practices.</h1><p class="gf-lede">Ground Floor is an independent project built around a local Apple Silicon lab. It exists to answer one narrow question honestly: can a particular documentation task be useful on hardware the practice controls?</p></div></header>
  <div class="gf-content"><div class="gf-shell grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_280px] gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-start">
    <article class="gf-prose">
      <h2>What does Ground Floor do?</h2>
      <p>Ground Floor designs and documents local-AI field tests for repetitive work such as source-based drafts, meeting notes, intake summaries, and document triage. A qualified professional still reviews and owns the final work.</p>
      <p>The setup checker is available now as a planning tool. The regulated-workflow pages are currently protocols, not completed studies.</p>
      <h2>Why start with local processing?</h2>
      <p>A local runtime can remove a third-party model API from the data path. That is useful when the source material is sensitive. It does not automatically make a workflow secure, private, privileged, compliant, accurate, or appropriate.</p>
      <h2>Where does its authority stop?</h2>
      <p>Ground Floor’s authority is technical: hardware, runtimes, test design, retained outputs, and measurement. It does not provide legal, medical, compliance, financial, or tax advice.</p>
      <h2>How does Ground Floor communicate?</h2>
      <p>Start with the customer’s real task. Show what the tool does. State the limits beside the claim. Publish “not good enough” when that is what the evidence earns. Those rules matter more here than sounding visionary.</p>
      <h2>How can I get involved?</h2>
      <p>Bring one repetitive documentation task. Describe it without sending confidential material. If it is safe and evaluable, Ground Floor can help turn it into a test protocol.</p>
      <a class="gf-button mt-4" href="/pilot">Tell us the task</a>
    </article>
    <aside class="border-t-4 border-[#111820] pt-5 lg:sticky lg:top-24">
      <p class="gf-eyebrow">Project facts</p>
      <dl class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed mt-5">
        <dt class="text-[#63707a]">Current measured workflows</dt><dd class="mt-1 mb-5">0</dd>
        <dt class="text-[#63707a]">Published protocols</dt><dd class="mt-1 mb-5">3</dd>
        <dt class="text-[#63707a]">Business model</dt><dd class="mt-1 mb-5">Independent education and field testing; no software purchase required.</dd>
      </dl>
      <a class="gf-link text-[14px]" href="/scope">Read the full scope</a>
    </aside>
  </div></div>
</Base>
